Only children like Koala, free of
that history, can change the world.

269
00:16:36,280 --> 00:16:39,077
Please, you can't tell them.

270
00:16:39,160 --> 00:16:41,680
You have to hold it in.

271
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:46,740
Our tragedy and our hatred,
they must die with us.

272
00:16:47,120 --> 00:16:48,460
No, it's all wrong.

273
00:16:48,640 --> 00:16:49,480
You heard me.

274
00:16:53,220 --> 00:16:55,740
Some humans are kind.

275
00:16:56,120 --> 00:16:58,980
They know we're not so different.

276
00:16:59,320 --> 00:17:00,637
I know it too.

277
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:04,400
And because I've met so
many compassionate humans,

278
00:17:04,660 --> 00:17:09,600
I realize it's foolish to leave nothing
but hatred as legacy when I die.

279
00:17:10,120 --> 00:17:12,980
But even though my mind understands that,

280
00:17:13,260 --> 00:17:16,960
there is a devil in my
heart that cannot forgive,

281
00:17:17,360 --> 00:17:19,460
that fills me with rage.

282
00:17:20,740 --> 00:17:23,020
My very flesh rejects them.

283
00:17:23,320 --> 00:17:25,240
It rejects their blood.

284
00:17:27,320 --> 00:17:33,440
Despite all that I fought for
I cannot love them I'm sorry.

285
00:17:35,480 --> 00:17:38,537
However you feel you can
work it out when this

286
00:17:38,620 --> 00:17:42,017
is all done for now I'm
begging you just live.

287
00:17:42,100 --> 00:17:45,757
Listen boss you're a
hero those slaves that

288
00:17:45,840 --> 00:17:48,517
you set free they owe
you their very lives.

289
00:17:48,600 --> 00:17:51,680
Please, boss, you can't
die. Not like this.

290
00:17:51,880 --> 00:17:55,660
To every slave and every
fishman, you're a symbol of hope.

291
00:17:56,780 --> 00:17:57,980
Then I'm happy.

292
00:17:59,660 --> 00:18:02,280
You're still not strong enough. Damn it!

293
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:06,500
You have to step in front of your
men with your whole body. Do that.

294
00:18:06,660 --> 00:18:08,280
You protect them. Huh?

295
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:09,880
Why would I...

296
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:12,150
Jinbei!

297
00:18:12,260 --> 00:18:14,848
If there's no one else
who can challenge me,

298
00:18:15,140 --> 00:18:17,397
I'm the new leader of
the fishman district.

299
00:18:17,480 --> 00:18:19,540
Call me Tiger!

300
00:18:20,520 --> 00:18:21,960
We're all brothers now.

301
00:18:22,780 --> 00:18:24,300
Your blood is my blood.

302
00:18:24,580 --> 00:18:27,100
So I swear that I'll protect it.

303
00:18:28,060 --> 00:18:30,820
I'll fight for the
lives of every fish man.

304
00:18:52,840 --> 00:18:53,670
Nooooooo!

305
00:18:58,640 --> 00:18:59,470
Nooooooooooo!

306
00:19:07,980 --> 00:19:09,900
Sorry, Tiger, but you're wrong!

307
00:19:10,220 --> 00:19:12,120
I'll never forgive them!

308
00:19:23,640 --> 00:19:25,400
All right, you punks!

309
00:19:25,540 --> 00:19:27,880
Get ready to die! A fish man?

310
00:19:28,040 --> 00:19:29,099
He must be from...

311
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:38,940
He's awful noisy, isn't he?

312
00:19:48,520 --> 00:19:49,980
Far along, was it?

313
00:19:51,660 --> 00:19:53,360
So what brings you here?

314
00:19:54,240 --> 00:19:56,420
You want to start trouble that bad?

315
00:20:05,040 --> 00:20:07,200
Not too smart, if you ask me.

316
00:20:07,680 --> 00:20:08,560
Out of my way!

317
00:20:08,720 --> 00:20:11,917
I'm going after all the lousy
humans who betrayed my captain!

318
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:14,300
And you, Navy scum, can't stop me!

319
00:20:14,640 --> 00:20:16,840
Oh, so this is about revenge.

320
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:18,310
Damn straight!

321
00:20:18,540 --> 00:20:20,100
You killed Fisher Tiger!

322
00:20:20,400 --> 00:20:23,557
I don't care what happens to
me, but you deserve to die!

323
00:20:23,640 --> 00:20:26,400
Oh, so your friend is dead, I see.

324
00:20:27,360 --> 00:20:31,660
Well, you can cry if you like, but
either way, you're coming with me now.

325
00:20:35,680 --> 00:20:38,300
Arlong was enraged by
Brother Tiger's death.

326
00:20:38,900 --> 00:20:42,840
He took his anger out on humans
and was imprisoned as a result.

327
00:20:43,320 --> 00:20:44,920
There his hatred grew.

328
00:20:47,480 --> 00:20:50,460
If he had a transfusion, he'd be fine.

329
00:20:50,720 --> 00:20:54,367
Instead, he had to die, because
they refused to treat fishmen.

330
00:20:54,520 --> 00:20:59,402
He brought that little girl back to her
family, and you repaid that by killing him!

331
00:21:01,500 --> 00:21:04,380
Fisher Tiger, captain of the Sun Pirates,

332
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:07,798
dies after being denied a
transfusion of human blood.

333
00:21:08,860 --> 00:21:11,100
Not quite, though it is close.

334
00:21:13,080 --> 00:21:16,297
Regardless, the captain's dead,
and humans played a big role.

335
00:21:16,380 --> 00:21:17,700
Arlong lied to them.

336
00:21:18,180 --> 00:21:19,597
Why would he do such a thing?

337
00:21:19,680 --> 00:21:20,520
Good for him.

338
00:21:20,880 --> 00:21:22,351
The truth is a lot worse.

339
00:21:22,760 --> 00:21:25,817
Tiger chose to save that girl
despite his own prejudice.

340
00:21:25,900 --> 00:21:29,977
Yet humans still betrayed him, so he
coldly refused to accept their blood.

341
00:21:30,060 --> 00:21:31,884
On top of that, he was a slave.

342
00:21:32,140 --> 00:21:36,434
If any of this became public, they
would have attacked Tiger's character.

343
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:40,120
So let Arlong tell his little white lies.

344
00:21:45,960 --> 00:21:46,790
You!

345
00:21:46,873 --> 00:21:48,237
Hey, Captain Jinbei!

346
00:21:48,320 --> 00:21:49,420
Enemy ship ahead!

347
00:21:49,800 --> 00:21:53,918
The boss may not be with us, but we
still have to keep moving forward.

348
00:21:55,760 --> 00:21:56,897
Prepare yourselves!

349
00:21:56,980 --> 00:22:00,120
Follow Tiger's wishes and
do not kill anyone! Yeah!

350
00:22:03,860 --> 00:22:05,380
From that day forward,

351
00:22:05,840 --> 00:22:09,217
I bore the title First
Son of the Sea and fought

352
00:22:09,300 --> 00:22:11,888
to do my best as Captain
of the Sun Pirates.

353
00:22:12,380 --> 00:22:16,674
Though in truth, fighting seemed to
be the only thing our crew was doing.

354
00:22:18,540 --> 00:22:22,597
I am writing this because
I thought the two of you

355
00:22:22,680 --> 00:22:25,798
deserved to know the whole
truth about what happened.

356
00:22:27,100 --> 00:22:29,960
Signed, Jinbei, Captain
of the Sun Pirates.

357
00:22:31,000 --> 00:22:32,420
My mind's made up.

358
00:22:33,600 --> 00:22:37,920
In the end, Fisher Tiger lived
the only way that he knew how.

359
00:22:38,940 --> 00:22:43,640
Poor Saul, I finally understand
the pain that he felt that day.

360
00:22:56,380 --> 00:22:58,760
As their leader, I must remain strong.

361
00:22:59,520 --> 00:23:00,697
I won't give in!

362
00:23:00,780 --> 00:23:06,517
We too shall live under the Sun
and try to understand one another!

363
00:23:06,600 --> 00:23:11,997
If I may, signing here is the first
step to harmony with all due respect.

364
00:23:12,080 --> 00:23:14,257
We know, to he may, you
must be out of your mind!

365
00:23:14,340 --> 00:23:17,217
Fisher Tiger freed countless
slaves, both fishmen and human.

366
00:23:17,300 --> 00:23:19,077
He didn't care about what race they were.

367
00:23:19,160 --> 00:23:21,577
Yet humans still refused to help him.

368
00:23:21,660 --> 00:23:27,677
Who cares about understanding another?

369
00:23:27,760 --> 00:23:29,877
Fruitless day without any signatures.

370
00:23:29,960 --> 00:23:32,677
Mother,

371
00:23:32,760 --> 00:23:39,760
you

372
00:23:44,800 --> 00:23:45,630
really

373
00:23:45,713 --> 00:23:46,543
need some rest.

374
00:23:46,626 --> 00:23:49,717
You children brighten my day.

375
00:23:49,800 --> 00:23:52,257
I'm fine!

376
00:23:52,340 --> 00:23:53,177
Don't worry.

377
00:23:53,260 --> 00:23:55,777
Okay, I won't.

378
00:23:55,860 --> 00:23:59,760
If you say so, mother,
I'll keep doing my best

379
00:24:00,760 --> 00:24:03,677
to make this world a
better place for everyone.

380
00:24:03,760 --> 00:24:10,220
Queen Otohime was working
so hard, day after day.

381
00:24:18,420 --> 00:24:20,640
She rescued humans from shipwrecks.

382
00:24:24,060 --> 00:24:25,480
Are you all right?

383
00:24:25,720 --> 00:24:27,308
Pirates must have hit them.

384
00:24:27,920 --> 00:24:29,460
Please help me.

385
00:24:29,600 --> 00:24:31,012
Don't worry, we're here.

386
00:24:31,100 --> 00:24:32,982
Bring the wounded to the island.

387
00:24:33,560 --> 00:24:36,678
She taught the island children
about the world above.

388
00:24:37,780 --> 00:24:41,486
Does anybody remember what this
area with many trees is called?

389
00:24:41,820 --> 00:24:43,100
You there, forest.

390
00:24:43,600 --> 00:24:44,776
Like the sea forest.

391
00:24:45,240 --> 00:24:46,960
And collected signatures.

392
00:24:48,060 --> 00:24:49,180
Please, wait!

393
00:24:50,820 --> 00:24:53,160
I just need a moment of your time!

394
00:24:58,620 --> 00:24:59,450
However...

395
00:24:59,533 --> 00:25:00,440
Queen Otohime!

396
00:25:01,540 --> 00:25:02,370
Oh!

397
00:25:02,660 --> 00:25:03,660
Hello again!

398
00:25:04,120 --> 00:25:07,002
Thank you for showing your
support the other day.

399
00:25:07,300 --> 00:25:10,157
Actually, about that, we're curious.

400
00:25:10,240 --> 00:25:12,260
How many signatures do you have?

401
00:25:12,420 --> 00:25:14,757
Well, I've been collecting
them for five years now.

402
00:25:14,840 --> 00:25:19,134
One hundred sheets have been signed,
with each containing ten signatures.

403
00:25:19,440 --> 00:25:21,969
So that adds up to one
thousand supporters.

404
00:25:22,600 --> 00:25:27,012
Still, the population of the island is
five million, so we're not done yet.

405
00:25:27,200 --> 00:25:28,400
Step by step, right?

406
00:25:30,780 --> 00:25:33,880
Um, we have kind of a big favor to ask.

407
00:25:34,040 --> 00:25:35,957
We'd like to withdraw our signatures.

408
00:25:36,040 --> 00:25:38,480
They total about half of what you have.

409
00:25:38,840 --> 00:25:41,037
Does that sound okay? Huh?

410
00:25:41,120 --> 00:25:42,897
You must not have heard about it,

411
00:25:42,980 --> 00:25:46,460
but those human pirates that
you rescued the other day?

412
00:25:48,280 --> 00:25:52,104
They committed a robbery in town
before escaping from the island.

413
00:26:00,780 --> 00:26:01,900
Your Majesty.

414
00:26:02,460 --> 00:26:03,340
Queen Otohime!

415
00:26:04,300 --> 00:26:05,177
Oh, hello, children.

416
00:26:05,260 --> 00:26:07,436
Are you ready for another lesson yet?

417
00:26:09,440 --> 00:26:10,300
Excuse me!

418
00:26:11,300 --> 00:26:14,217
My mom wants that paper I
signed the other day back.

419
00:26:14,300 --> 00:26:15,940
I found it! Yeah!

420
00:26:16,720 --> 00:26:17,600
Go, mommy!

421
00:26:24,300 --> 00:26:25,480
May I help you?

422
00:26:25,760 --> 00:26:27,637
I do hope there's no hard feelings.

423
00:26:27,720 --> 00:26:29,955
What with you being the queen and all.

424
00:26:31,720 --> 00:26:33,100
We just can't do it.

425
00:26:33,560 --> 00:26:34,820
Humans are too evil.

426
00:26:36,900 --> 00:26:38,657
We'll pass on the speeches, too.

427
00:26:38,740 --> 00:26:41,140
Yeah, sorry about all this.

428
00:26:43,740 --> 00:26:45,140
We've just had enough.

429
00:26:53,600 --> 00:26:54,720
Surprise, Mommy!

430
00:26:55,160 --> 00:26:56,260
Did we scare you?

431
00:26:58,480 --> 00:27:00,200
What an exhausting day.

432
00:27:00,620 --> 00:27:03,117
I think I might have
overdone it a bit out there.

433
00:27:03,200 --> 00:27:07,553
I'm sorry, sweeties, but could you
give your mother some alone time today?

434
00:27:29,400 --> 00:27:30,717
You...

435
00:27:30,800 --> 00:27:32,557
You're all...

436
00:27:32,640 --> 00:27:34,240
Liars!

437
00:27:36,060 --> 00:27:38,980
Your Majesty, this is on the air.

438
00:27:39,260 --> 00:27:41,000
Everyone can hear you.

439
00:27:43,760 --> 00:27:45,980
Why don't you shut up?

440
00:27:47,540 --> 00:27:48,370
Mr.

441
00:27:48,453 --> 00:27:49,440
At the Left!

442
00:27:53,080 --> 00:27:55,100
Majesty, have you been drinking?

443
00:27:55,600 --> 00:27:56,720
Leave me alone.

444
00:27:57,140 --> 00:27:59,800
I'm not drunk at all.

445
00:28:00,220 --> 00:28:03,157
Yes, you are. Goodness. What's happening?

446
00:28:03,240 --> 00:28:05,540
Is that really Queen Otohime?

447
00:28:05,980 --> 00:28:08,220
Everybody better listen to me!

448
00:28:08,820 --> 00:28:11,080
You can live however you want.

449
00:28:11,420 --> 00:28:13,680
If that means staying in this island,

450
00:28:13,860 --> 00:28:16,625
then I can't stop you,
neither can anyone else.

451
00:28:17,000 --> 00:28:20,700
But in the vastness of
the ocean, so broad.

452
00:28:21,500 --> 00:28:24,700
And on the sea floor, foreboding and dark.

453
00:28:28,260 --> 00:28:31,920
We chose this tiny place
and this place alone.

454
00:28:32,660 --> 00:28:34,240
Do you have any idea why?

455
00:28:36,080 --> 00:28:40,580
Queen Otohime, isn't it because this
is where we can get a bit of sunlight?

456
00:28:40,880 --> 00:28:42,645
Where we can get a bit of air?

457
00:28:43,560 --> 00:28:46,266
Luxuries down here are
plentiful above ground.

458
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:48,797
Light illuminates the entire surface,

459
00:28:48,880 --> 00:28:52,200
and the sky stretches out
as far as you can see.

460
00:28:58,560 --> 00:29:04,440
Our children why do they always sneak
out to catch a glimpse of Sabo Ori Park?

461
00:29:07,620 --> 00:29:11,817
Can't you see the world is filled with

462
00:29:11,900 --> 00:29:14,860
more beauty than any
of us can even imagine?

463
00:29:15,580 --> 00:29:17,817
There's no place that we shouldn't be able

464
00:29:17,900 --> 00:29:21,340
to go why restrict
ourselves to this bubble?

465
00:29:22,200 --> 00:29:26,494
I know you tell yourselves life down
here is comfortable but you're safe.

466
00:29:27,240 --> 00:29:30,057
Do you want to spend the
rest of your lives trapped?

467
00:29:30,140 --> 00:29:33,480
dig deep summon your courage.

468
00:29:34,580 --> 00:29:38,037
Once you have it pursue
your dreams no matter

469
00:29:38,120 --> 00:29:44,077
the cost your majesty if
humans stand in your way?

470
00:29:44,160 --> 00:29:50,097
We'll face them together you don't have to
confront your fears alone and maybe then?

471
00:29:50,180 --> 00:29:56,360
We can finally make a difference for the
future, for our children, for the island.

472
00:29:58,360 --> 00:30:00,740
Even if it's just a small one.

473
00:30:15,980 --> 00:30:18,677
My goodness, you've seen better days.

474
00:30:18,760 --> 00:30:20,200
He was formidable.

475
00:30:20,980 --> 00:30:21,810
I see.

476
00:30:22,040 --> 00:30:24,628
He certainly did a
number on you, didn't he?

477
00:30:26,240 --> 00:30:30,769
Arlong, the fishman that we just locked
up and impelled down, he was nothing.

478
00:30:31,220 --> 00:30:33,514
But you have to watch out for this one.

479
00:30:33,740 --> 00:30:34,570
Jinbei!

480
00:30:39,100 --> 00:30:42,020
He's quite strong, even
by fishman standards.

481
00:30:42,920 --> 00:30:44,900
He's far too dangerous at large.

482
00:30:45,100 --> 00:30:46,453
We should bring him in.

483
00:30:54,340 --> 00:30:55,170
Unbelievable.

484
00:30:55,253 --> 00:30:56,500
Me and the seven warlords?

485
00:30:56,800 --> 00:30:58,506
Oh, it's not that surprising.

486
00:30:58,720 --> 00:31:00,640
You're worth $250 million.

487
00:31:01,040 --> 00:31:04,817
With a bounty that big, they definitely see
you as a threat to the world government.

488
00:31:04,900 --> 00:31:08,117
That's the highest praise a
pirate can get from those chumps.

489
00:31:08,200 --> 00:31:09,030
Mackerel's right.

490
00:31:09,113 --> 00:31:11,198
They're finally taking us seriously.

491
00:31:11,320 --> 00:31:13,257
All you need to do is reject them.

492
00:31:13,340 --> 00:31:15,987
That'll really help us
pile on the notoriety.

493
00:31:16,220 --> 00:31:17,985
No one will ever mess with us.

494
00:31:18,720 --> 00:31:20,440
My mind is made up.

495
00:31:20,980 --> 00:31:23,640
I'm going to take the navy's offer! What?

496
00:31:25,040 --> 00:31:26,497
Welcome home, Jinbei.

497
00:31:26,580 --> 00:31:29,700
I heard about the seven
warlords' proposal.

498
00:31:30,380 --> 00:31:31,537
If I join,

499
00:31:31,620 --> 00:31:33,517
Aladdin and the other crew members Who do

500
00:31:33,600 --> 00:31:35,917
not wish to be pirates
No longer have to be.

501
00:31:36,000 --> 00:31:38,877
They can live in this country
without fear of retribution.

502
00:31:38,960 --> 00:31:41,380
It's a way for me to take care of my men.

503
00:31:41,980 --> 00:31:45,177
But more importantly If
I do become a warlord?

504
00:31:45,260 --> 00:31:48,777
It will help the fishermen become
closer to the world government.

505
00:31:48,860 --> 00:31:50,389
We need that relationship.

506
00:31:51,000 --> 00:31:54,529
I can atone for all the trouble
that we've caused the Queen.

507
00:31:55,060 --> 00:31:55,980
Thank you.

508
00:31:56,980 --> 00:32:00,920
At the moment, she's
not feeling very well.

509
00:32:02,460 --> 00:32:05,200
In the end, we might see Tiger's dream.

510
00:32:05,900 --> 00:32:09,018
Liberation and freedom for
all fishermen, everywhere.

511
00:32:10,080 --> 00:32:13,257
Though, then again, we
have to watch our own.

512
00:32:13,340 --> 00:32:16,500
There are some less deserving of amnesty.

513
00:32:22,440 --> 00:32:23,270
Arlong!

514
00:32:27,480 --> 00:32:28,980
It's really new!

515
00:32:31,420 --> 00:32:33,760
So good to have your back, bro!

516
00:32:37,920 --> 00:32:41,677
If you have something to say to
me, then you'd better speak up now.

517
00:32:41,760 --> 00:32:45,360
Now, you expect to thank
you for becoming a sellout.

518
00:32:45,660 --> 00:32:49,780
You may have set me free,
but the Navy owns you.

519
00:32:50,180 --> 00:32:53,415
Have you forgotten what
Brother Ty said before he died?

520
00:32:53,800 --> 00:32:56,800
You mustn't let anger and
bitterness overwhelm you.

521
00:32:58,280 --> 00:33:00,456
Sounds to me like you've gotten soft.

522
00:33:00,840 --> 00:33:03,337
Sure, I'd probably be safer
if I followed your lead,

523
00:33:03,420 --> 00:33:05,377
but there's no way in hell I'm doing that.

524
00:33:05,460 --> 00:33:06,900
You can't make me sick.

525
00:33:07,500 --> 00:33:10,280
In case you forgot, Tiger is dead.

526
